quiet.md #17: single-axis scrollers take only gestures that lean their way

In a container that scrolls on one axis only, a scroll event counts only if
it moves more along that axis than across it. Otherwise a vertical mouse
wheel over a wide table was turned into sideways scrolling, and the small
sideways drift of a vertical trackpad swipe slid the table while the page
scrolled (the concurrent-scroll lock never fires there, one delta being
zero). Upstream's opt-in restrict_scroll_to_axis only locks trackpad
gestures for containers with a tracked scroll handle.

